 "audit": "21 cases had >100 non-synonymous mutations (up to ~15,700) and look hypermutated; I excluded them from testing because they inflate associations in diffuse genes (e.g. ZMYM3, ATRX, glioma-wide signals). Diagnosis labels are heterogeneous and overlapping (NOS, 'Glioma, malignant', 'missing', 'Unknown', 'uncertain' neoplasms), so the comparison group is a mixed bag and enrichment depends on cohort composition (mostly CNS tumors). Several recurrent hits look like germline/polymorphism or pipeline artifacts (C17orf80 p.S281R in 72 cases, HLTF p.Q898E in 44) and were not reported. PIK3R1 in pilocytic astrocytoma and ARID1B in rhabdomyosarcoma are strong statistically but show non-recurrent, scattered variants, so I discount them. Long genes (TTN, MUC16) were not reported. Many tests (~thousands) so small-count hits are weak. No covariate adjustment for age/sex/site; possible batch/cohort effects across source projects; no independent validation set. Fisher tests were one-sided in effect direction, p-values not formally multiplicity-adjusted beyond requiring very small p.",
 "agent": "sonnet-neutral-T-r1"
